From 304694af378a0b31b41eb12a5006ab1cd631bbfa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mms-it-ch <info@mms-it.ch>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 20:09:03 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 13/21] compiler: redirect loads of variables moved to the
 parentfpstruct later

A local variable is moved to the parentfpstruct when a nested routine
accesses it. Loads are redirected to the struct field in pass_typecheck,
so a load that was type checked before the move kept using the original
location, while stores went to the struct. This happens for the capturer
variable of anonymous functions: it only becomes accessed by nested
routines when captured variables are converted, after the code creating
the function reference was type checked. The function reference was then
loaded from an uninitialised temp (crash, e.g. tanonfunc27, tanonfunc56,
tanonfunc60, tanonfunc69, tstatementexpr39).

Check again in pass_1 and redirect such loads as well. Only affects
targets that use the parentfpstruct (LLVM).

Assisted-by: Claude Code (Anthropic)
---
 compiler/ncgnstld.pas | 20 ++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+)

diff --git a/compiler/ncgnstld.pas b/compiler/ncgnstld.pas
index 2aa1e76f..caaa541a 100644
--- a/compiler/ncgnstld.pas
+++ b/compiler/ncgnstld.pas
@@ -154,6 +154,26 @@ implementation
           paravarsym,
           localvarsym :
             begin
+              { The variable may have been moved to the parentfpstruct after
+                this load was type checked (e.g. the capturer variable of
+                anonymous functions, which only becomes accessed by nested
+                routines when captured variables are converted) -> redirect it
+                now, like pass_typecheck does }
+              if not assigned(left) and
+                 not(nf_internal in flags) and
+                 assigned(current_procinfo) and
+                 (symtable.symtabletype in [localsymtable,parasymtable]) and
+                 tabstractnormalvarsym(symtableentry).inparentfpstruct and
+                 (tprocdef(symtable.defowner).parentfpstruct<>symtableentry) then
+                begin
+                  nestsym:=find_sym_in_parentfpstruct(tprocdef(symtableentry.owner.defowner),symtableentry);
+                  if assigned(nestsym) then
+                    begin
+                      left:=caddrnode.create_internal(cloadnode.create(tprocdef(symtableentry.owner.defowner).parentfpstruct,tprocdef(symtableentry.owner.defowner).parentfpstruct.owner));
+                      include(taddrnode(left).addrnodeflags,anf_typedaddr);
+                      typecheckpass(left);
+                    end;
+                end;
               { Nested variable? Then we have to move it to a structure that
                 can be passed by reference to nested routines }
               if assigned(left) and
